<!-- Compact homepage FAQ accordion (full-width) -->
<section id="faq" class="py-5 cf-faq-fullbleed">
  <div class="cf-faq-accordion">
    <div class="cf-faq-list">
      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q1">
        <summary>
          What is CogniFocus?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            CogniFocus is a focus timer and app blocker that combines a
            Distraction Shield, a reactive Goblin character, XP and streak
            tracking, and recovery nudges. It is designed for people who find
            traditional focus timers too passive &mdash; the kind of people who
            start a session, drift into Instagram anyway, and need something
            that actually reacts before one scroll becomes thirty minutes.
            <span class="visually-hidden">
              CogniFocus is a focus timer and app blocker that combines a
              Distraction Shield, a reactive Goblin character, XP and streak
              tracking, and recovery nudges. It is designed for people who find
              traditional focus timers too passive &mdash; the kind of people
              who start a session, drift into Instagram anyway, and need
              something that actually reacts before one scroll becomes thirty
              minutes.
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q2">
        <summary>
          How is it different from a normal timer?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            A normal timer counts down and stops. CogniFocus actively watches
            what you do during a session. If you drift into TikTok, Instagram,
            or YouTube, the Distraction Shield interrupts the app and the
            Goblin reacts &mdash; giving you a moment of accountability before
            the scroll takes over. Sessions build streaks, XP, and companion
            affinity over time, so focus becomes something you build, not just
            something you attempt.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q3">
        <summary>
          What happens if I open TikTok or Instagram?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            The Distraction Shield detects the app switch and interrupts it
            before you get pulled in. The Goblin reacts based on how the session
            is going &mdash; annoyed, angry, or disappointed depending on the
            pattern. If you slip, the recovery system nudges you back into the
            session rather than treating one distraction as total failure. One
            bad moment does not have to end the session.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q4">
        <summary>
          Why does it need Android permissions?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            CogniFocus needs Usage Access permission to detect which app is in
            the foreground &mdash; this is what allows the Distraction Shield to
            react the moment you switch to a blocked app. It also needs Display
            Over Other Apps permission to show the Shield overlay. CogniFocus
            does not read your messages, access your contacts, or collect any
            private content. You can review the full breakdown in the Privacy
            Policy.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <p class="cf-faq-content visually-hidden">
        Distraction apps like TikTok and Instagram use variable reward schedules
        &mdash; the same mechanism as slot machines &mdash; to make opening them
        automatic. Most focus timers do not interrupt this loop. CogniFocus is
        built to intercept the moment of drift: the Distraction Shield activates
        when a blocked app is opened during a session, and the Goblin character
        provides an immediate behavioral cue before the scroll takes hold.
      </p>
      <p class="cf-faq-content visually-hidden">
        Recovery nudges matter because most people abandon a focus session after
        one distraction. CogniFocus treats a slip as a recovery opportunity
        rather than a failure &mdash; which supports better long-term consistency
        than strict all-or-nothing blocking.
      </p>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q5">
        <summary>
          Is CogniFocus available on iOS?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            Join the waitlist using the button above and you will be the first
            to know when it launches.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q6">
        <summary>
          Is CogniFocus available on Mac?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            No. CogniFocus is not available as a Mac app, Mac desktop app, or
            macOS focus timer. It is currently built for Android only.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q7">
        <summary>
          Is CogniFocus available on Windows?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            No. CogniFocus is not available as a Windows app or Windows desktop
            blocker. It is currently built for Android only.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q8">
        <summary>
          Is CogniFocus available on Chromebooks?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            Yes, on Chromebooks that support Android apps. If your Chromebook
            can run Android app blockers from the Play Store, CogniFocus may
            work there as a Chromebook focus app.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q9">
        <summary>
          What does Pro add?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            Pro unlocks stronger Distraction Shield capacity, Manual Block mode
            to lock specific apps outside of a session, planned session
            scheduling, focus reminders, and session restore support. Free users
            get the core focus timer, app blocking during sessions, Goblin
            reactions, and streak tracking. Pro is for people who want tighter
            control and longer-term habit support.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
